  "limitations": [
    "Curated reference only; this is not complete world history and does not claim full coverage of any country, city, person or period.",
    "Europe, and especially Vienna/Austria, is covered more deeply than Africa, Asia, Latin America and Oceania.",
    "Dates and periodization are simplified; borders, sovereignty and state identity changed repeatedly and are represented as index periods, not polygons.",
    "Most sources are tertiary references (Wikipedia) and structured data (Wikidata); primary archival verification was not performed for every date.",
    "Wikipedia/Wikidata, country, city and event URLs were checked on 2026-11-05. Official USHMM and IAEA pages blocked automated fetches from the build environment; their URLs are retained as canonical citations with verification=blocked.",
    "City coordinates are modern city-centre points rounded to four decimals, not historical urban extents.",
    "People records are identity anchors with no scripted fates, alliances or future actions.",
    "Inference records are explicit aggregate/synthesized conditions; they are not discrete events and should be checked against local archives before being treated as hard facts.",
    "Fiction hooks are counterfactual premises, are stored in a separate file and must never be loaded as reference or seeded as committed events."
  ]
